.TH AVR\-ORG\-SAML\-CONFIGURE 1 "" "avr 0.2.0" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-org-saml-configure \- Create or replace SAML configuration from IdP metadata (admin only).
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr org saml configure
[OPTIONS] METADATA
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create or replace SAML configuration from IdP metadata (admin only).
.PP
METADATA is an IdP metadata XML file; pass - to read it from stdin. Reconfiguring requires the complete metadata document again.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
Examples:
    avr org saml configure idp-metadata.xml
    cat idp-metadata.xml | avr org saml configure - --org acme
    avr org saml configure idp.xml --email-attribute mail \e
        --given-name-attribute firstName --family-name-attribute lastName
.fi
.RE
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
JSON FIELDS
    allow_idp_initiated, attr_email, attr_family_name, attr_given_name,
    attr_groups, created_at, default_role, idp_entity_id, idp_slo_url,
    idp_sso_url, is_enforced, jit_provisioning, name_id_format,
    organization_id, organization_saml_config_id, updated_at
.fi
.RE
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fIMETADATA\fR
\&
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID or slug. Uses default org if not specified (see: avr config set org).
.TP
\fB\-\-email\-attribute\fR, \fB\-\-attr\-email\fR \fITEXT\fR
IdP attribute carrying the member email. (default: email)
.TP
\fB\-\-given\-name\-attribute\fR, \fB\-\-attr\-given\-name\fR \fITEXT\fR
IdP given-name attribute.
.TP
\fB\-\-family\-name\-attribute\fR, \fB\-\-attr\-family\-name\fR \fITEXT\fR
IdP family-name attribute.
.TP
\fB\-\-groups\-attribute\fR, \fB\-\-attr\-groups\fR \fITEXT\fR
IdP groups attribute.
.TP
\fB\-\-default\-role\fR \fICHOICE\fR
Role assigned to JIT-provisioned members. (choices: user, admin, billing_admin; default: user)
.TP
\fB\-\-jit\-provisioning\fR / \fB\-\-no\-jit\-provisioning\fR
Allow SAML to provision new members. (default: True)
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-idp\-initiated\fR / \fB\-\-no\-allow\-idp\-initiated\fR
Allow sign-in initiated from the IdP.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR \fITEXT\fR
Output JSON. Pass comma-separated field names, "*" for all fields, or "?" to list available fields.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-jq\fR \fITEXT\fR
Filter --json output through a jq expression.
.SH SEE ALSO
